-- title:
--   Passage to the limit on the right-hand side of the discrete inequality
-- statement:
--   Let $d \ge 1$, let $\alpha \ge 0$ and $\Lambda \in \mathbb{R}$, and let
--
--   $$k : \mathbb{R}^d \times \mathbb{R}^d \to [0,\infty]$$
--
--   be jointly measurable in the pair and dominated by the fractional jump kernel,
--
--   $$k(a,b) \;\le\; \Lambda\,\lVert a-b\rVert^{-d-\alpha} \qquad \text{for all } a,b \in \mathbb{R}^d,$$
--
--   which is the upper half of the standing kernel bound (`jumpKernel d α a b` being $\lVert a-b\rVert^{-d-\alpha}$). Let $f : \mathbb{R}^d \to \mathbb{R}$ be measurable and locally integrable, let $x_0 \in \mathbb{R}^d$, and let $R, R' \in \mathbb{R}$ be radii. Let $(h_n)_{n \in \mathbb{N}}$ be a sequence of mesh sizes with
--
--   $$h_n > 0, \qquad h_n \to 0, \qquad \sqrt{d}\,\frac{h_n}{2} \;\le\; R' - R \quad \text{for every } n,$$
--
--   so that in particular $R < R'$. Write $\lVert u\rVert_\infty = \sup_i|u_i|$ and $\bar A_h(u) = \{s : \lVert s-u\rVert_\infty \le h/2\}$. Assume finally the *a priori* hypothesis that $f$ already has finite $H^{\alpha/2}$ energy on the larger ball,
--
--   $$|f|^2_{H^{\alpha/2}(B(x_0,R'))} \;=\; \iint_{B(x_0,R')^2} \bigl(f(t)-f(s)\bigr)^2 \lVert s-t\rVert^{-d-\alpha}\,d(s,t) \;\ne\; \infty .$$
--
--   Then
--
--   $$\limsup_{n \to \infty} \int_{\mathbb{R}^d \times \mathbb{R}^d} g_{h_n}(s,t)\,d(s,t) \;\le\; \mathcal{E}_k\big(B(x_0,R)\big)[f],$$
--
--   where, for a mesh $h$,
--   $$g_h(s,t) \;=\; \mathbf 1_{P_h}\bigl(\iota_h(s), \iota_h(t)\bigr)\,\bigl(f_h(\iota_h(s)) - f_h(\iota_h(t))\bigr)^2\, k(s,t)$$
--   is the paper's discretized integrand `stepG d h (ball x₀ R) (3·√d·h) k f`. Here $\iota_h(s) = \bigl(\operatorname{round}(s_i/h)\,h\bigr)_i$ is the lattice point of $h\mathbb{Z}^d$ whose tile contains $s$, $f_h(u) = \frac{1}{|\bar A_h(u)|}\int_{\bar A_h(u)} f$ is the average of $f$ over the closed cube of side $h$ centred at $u$, and
--   $$P_h \;=\; \bigl\{(u,w) : u, w \in B(x_0,R) \cap h\mathbb{Z}^d,\ \ 3\sqrt d\,h < \lVert u - w\rVert\bigr\}$$
--   is the set of admitted pairs of tile indices. Finally $\mathcal{E}_k(\Omega)[f] = \iint_{\Omega\times\Omega}\bigl(f(t)-f(s)\bigr)^2 k(s,t)\,d(s,t)$ is the $H_k$ energy of $f$ on $\Omega$, the quadratic form with kernel $k$ over $\Omega$.
--
--   This is the step that the source argument asserts by dominated convergence without exhibiting a dominating function; the result above supplies the passage to the limit under one extra hypothesis, namely the finiteness of the $H^{\alpha/2}$ energy of $f$ on the *enlarged* ball $B(x_0,R')$. That hypothesis is precisely what an appeal to dominated convergence needs here, and it is not available unconditionally.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The values are in `ℝ≥0∞` throughout, so both sides may be $+\infty$ and the inequality is still meaningful. No positivity is assumed of $R$ or of $\Lambda$; if $\Lambda < 0$ then `ENNReal.ofReal Λ = 0` and the kernel bound forces $k \equiv 0$, making the statement trivial in that degenerate case. The separation parameter is taken to be $3\sqrt d\,h$ rather than $\sqrt d\,h$, which only strengthens the constraint defining the support of $g_h$.
